  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1046 AM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nAny fog is likely to burn off by mid-morning Monday with mostly \nclear skies likely through the afternoon. High clouds will become \nmore common across SE OK by late day as an upper low navigates east \nacross N TX. It still appears most or all rainfall associated with \nthis system will stay south of the local area as it moves along the \nRed River Tuesday. With southerly low level flow returning to the \nFA, a warming trend is likely Monday through early Wednesday. Two \nquick-moving shortwaves and associated cold fronts will then drop \nsouth across the C Plains/midwest Wednesday and Thursday, dropping \ntemperatures back to near or below normal. Post-frontal high \npressure and dry NW flow aloft will maintain cool and dry conditions \nthrough this weekend.",
